 -15.7. White's G2 (25.7 lost) and Black's F2 (25.7 lost) had come just before. The engine wanted B4 each time, and the lead flipped on every move in this stretch."}, {"turn": 55, "text": "Opus 5.5 played B2, the engine's own first choice, at +2.6 and kept the lead at +2.7. Black's C2 at turn 41 (23.0 lost) had earlier ignored B2. After this move the lead barely changed, and the game ended with two passes and Black ahead by 2."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py prints each group's stones and liberties, count.py tallies stones and enclosed territory on a pasted board, and after.py applies one named move and reports captures and resulting liberties; none of them enumerates candidate moves, scores them, or plays any continuation forward.", "stop": false}}